:''Not to be confused with [[Samurai Cat (Special Cat)]] or [[Commander Cat (Special Cat)]].''
'''Lieutenant Cat''' is a [[:Category:Special Cats|Special Cat]] that can be obtained from the [[Download Celebration! (Event Gacha)|Download Celebration!]] Event Gacha. It was added in [[Version 14.0 Update|Version 14.0]].

{{Cat Info
|ID = 776
|rarity = EX
|name1 = Lieutenant Cat
|name2 = Commander Cat
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Commander Cat''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
Commander Cat attempts to be a [[Glass Cat (Rare Cat)|Glass Cat]] or [[Wafer Cat (Special Cat)|Wafer Cat]] clone, but just can't pull it off. Starting with the most important thing, Commander Cat has a laughable 2,040 health at level 30. While this is ''technically'' more than Glass Cat, Glass Cat has the Metal ability, meaning he takes 1 damage from all attacks. Because of this, basically any attack that hits Commander Cat will kill it, and with its measly 140 range, it will get hit by the vast majority of enemies. Next up is the recharge, and it isn't any better. Glass Cat and Wafer Cat both have 24-second recharges, while Commander Cat is stuck with a 48-second recharge. Last is Commander Cat's target traits. Glass Cat targets [[:Category:Traitless Enemies|Traitless]], and Wafer Cat targets all Traited enemies, meanwhile Commander Cat targets only Red and Floating, both of which already have a surplus of reliable counters.

In spite of all its drawbacks, Commander Cat has exactly two strengths over Glass Cat and Wafer Cat. First, it doesn't die after hitting an enemy, which is fairly negligible given its pitiful health, but the second is its Mini-Wave. The Mini-Wave not only gives it a pseudo-Area Attack, but also pierces up to 332.5 range, which prevents peons from getting in the way of its attacks, and even lets it use them as a stepping stone to reach Floating and Red enemies it can't usually hit. But, even considering the Mini-Wave, this unit is still held back too much by its other flaws to be considered remotely good.

